p.src:
The interviewee now sharpens the point. These crimes, she says, were not just committed by individuals; they were committed by an entire society. That is the argument’s cleanest structural step: $\text{collective crime}
\Longrightarrow
\text{collective responsibility}.$ The claim is severe. If the crime belongs to a society as society, then the moral reckoning cannot be exhausted by tracing the guilt of separate persons one by one.

