p.src:
Aristotle enters exactly here, as the alternative: $\begin{aligned}
\text{politics}
&\neq
\text{maximizing GDP},\\
\text{politics}
&\Longrightarrow
\text{the good life}.\end{aligned}$ Sandel places this alternative historically as well: $2500\ \text{years ago}
\Longrightarrow
\text{ancient Athens as a demanding model of citizenship}.$ The provided transcript stops at the threshold of Aristotle, but the direction is already clear. Politics is about more than administration, protection, or economic management; it concerns the shape of a worthy common life.

